 ## Overview
-A CUDA kernel that maps 3D LiDAR points to a voxel grid by aggregating attributes into a block-level shared memory cache, falling back to atomic operations on global memory for cache collisions [S1, unofficial]. It differs from standard global-memory-only voxelization by reducing global memory contention through a small, fixed-size cache per block, and from pure shared-memory approaches by handling hash collisions gracefully [S1, unofficial].
+A CUDA kernel that maps 3D LiDAR points to a voxel grid by aggregating attributes into a block-level shared memory cache, falling back to atomic operations on global memory for cache collisions [S1, unofficial]. It reduces global memory contention compared to standard global-memory-only voxelization by using a fixed-size per-block cache, while gracefully handling hash collisions that pure shared-memory approaches cannot [S1, unofficial].
 
